@startuml file-lifecycle
' The lifecycle of a files.file row (docs/api/files/files.md §2). The state follows from etag, scanned_at and deleted_at;
' the row has no status column. Edge labels are kept short: the Smetana layout clips long ones at the canvas edge.
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    BorderColor #1E3A5F
    FontColor #1E3A5F
    AttributeFontColor #555555
    AttributeFontSize 11
}

title Lifecycle of a file

state Pending : etag IS NULL\nreaped after a day\nif never confirmed
state Confirmed : etag set\nscanned_at IS NULL
state Clean #E8F5E9 : etag and scanned_at set\n**downloadable by staff**
state Released #FFF3E0 : deleted_at set\nkept 7 days
state Reaped #EEEEEE : object and row deleted\nby FileJanitor
state Purged #EEEEEE : object and row deleted\nby FileJanitor

[*] --> Pending : POST /files/uploads

Pending --> Confirmed : reference committed,\nobject checks out
Pending --> Reaped : after a day,\nunconfirmed

Confirmed --> Clean : ClamAV: clean
Confirmed --> Released : ClamAV: infected\n(object deleted)

Clean --> Released : reference\nremoved

Released --> Purged : after 7 days

Reaped --> [*]
Purged --> [*]

@enduml
